  "note": "County council election of 1920 (proportional representation); polling day 5 June 1920. Returned unopposed. Portadown electoral area (four seats): the electoral divisions of Annaghmore, Breagh, Drumcree, Killyman, Portadown Rural and Tartaraghan and the urban district of Portadown. Four candidates for four seats: \"No contest\" (Newry Reporter, 1 May 1920, p. 3); the only area in the county without a contest (Belfast News-Letter, 6 May 1920, p. 3). No party labels printed."
